    "title": "TinCaps whipped by Whitecaps for second straight night, 11-1 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Josh Ayen ,\n1 hours ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – Fort Wayne’s pivotal homestand against West Michigan is off to a horrendous start following Wednesday’s 11-1 loss to the Whitecaps.\nIn two games this week to West Michigan, the TinCaps have been outscored 23-6 to the Whitecaps.\nWinyer Chourio suffered his fourth loss since being called up to the TinCaps halfway through the season. The righty allowed six runs on five hits and four walks, over two and two-thirds innings. Chourio allowed three home runs over the first two innings as West Michigan blew the game open with a 6-0 lead midway through the third inning.\nFort Wayne’s offense went cold on Wednesday, only collecting one run on five hits. Ryan Wideman drove in Kasen Wells for the TinCaps’ only run of the night in the bottom of the third inning.\nThe TinCaps look to snap a two-game skid on Thursday. First pitch is scheduled for 7:05 p.m. at Parkview Field.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
